# Force LF in the repository *and* in every working tree, on every platform.
#
# This is load-bearing, not cosmetic. Ingestion detects changed documents by
# hashing file bytes, and citation highlighting uses character offsets into the
# chunk text. Under Git's default autocrlf on Windows, a clone would produce
# CRLF while a macOS or Linux clone produces LF — the same document would hash
# differently per platform, so every file would look "changed" on first ingest,
# and highlight offsets would drift by one per preceding line.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets — never touch these
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.webp binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary

# Lockfile: generated, so keep it out of review diffs
pnpm-lock.yaml linguist-generated=true -diff
